<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00620">
	<title>Emergency Stop malfunction</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03869">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03870">
								<image href="images/OLQ2A005123.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03871">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Check Emergency Stopping function.</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When <uicontrol>Emergency Stop</uicontrol> is not working properly, the warning message and Master warning light (<image align="left" href="images/WKIA_040.jpg" scale="15" placement="inline"/>) will appear on the cluster. If this occurs, have your vehicle inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
		<note type="tip" id="e03872">
			<p>You can check the malfunction in the service message of the utility information view of the cluster display window.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
	<related-links>
		<linkpool>
			<link format="dita" href="t00619.dita#t00619" role="parent" scope="local" type="concept">
				<linktext>Emergency Stop malfunction and limitation</linktext>
			</link>
		</linkpool>
	</related-links>
</concept>